import{_ as e,o as t,c as a,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 563 | Time Ethics | Individual-Rights Protection in the Time Domain","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 563 | Time Ethics | Individual-Rights Protection in the Time Domain","no":563,"module":3,"tags":["Time Ethics","Individual Rights","Time Autonomy","Informed Consent","Myriad-Rank Republicanism"],"related":["19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries","26-Individual-Collective Balance Principle","40-Symbiotic Constitution Preamble","88-Cross-Plane Ethical Principle"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0563_模块3-时间伦理-时间域中的个体权利保障.md","filePath":"en/0563_模块3-时间伦理-时间域中的个体权利保障.md"}'),o={name:"en/0563_模块3-时间伦理-时间域中的个体权利保障.md"};function l(r,i,s,d,h,c){return t(),a("div",null,[...i[0]||(i[0]=[n('<h1 id="entry-563-time-ethics-individual-rights-protection-in-the-time-domain" tabindex="-1">Entry 563 | Time Ethics | Individual-Rights Protection in the Time Domain <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-563-time-ethics-individual-rights-protection-in-the-time-domain" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 563 | Time Ethics | Individual-Rights Protection in the Time Domain&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 3 · Dual-Track Time Domain Civilizational-Experience System | Benchmark base: Documents 19, 26, 40, 88</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-when-civilization-can-manipulate-time-on-what-basis-is-the-individual-not-treated-as-time-s-material" tabindex="-1">Introduction: when civilization can manipulate time, on what basis is the individual not treated as time&#39;s material <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-when-civilization-can-manipulate-time-on-what-basis-is-the-individual-not-treated-as-time-s-material" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: when civilization can manipulate time, on what basis is the individual not treated as time&#39;s material&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The dual-track time domain is a civilizational-level public project, but it is entered, experienced, borne by concrete individuals. No matter how grand the project, it may not dispatch the individual as &quot;time&#39;s material.&quot; The time-ethics special topic must specifically cover <strong>individual-rights protection</strong>: in a civilization able to adjust time, arrange trials, share consciousness, what inviolable rights does an ordinary being retain over his own time. This is the Individual-Collective Balance Principle (Document 26) concretized in the time dimension.</p><p>Six top-level axioms run through: republican axiom of Myriad Races is this entry&#39;s protagonist — the individual&#39;s time rights do not disappear because of the collective&#39;s grandeur; anti-predation axiom forbids plundering individual time into public material; collective ascension axiom emphasizes lifting the individual is the collective&#39;s purpose not means; causal self-discipline axiom respects individual causal autonomy; law-first axiom writes individual rights into law, not temporarily canceled for collective needs. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-four-fundamental-rights-of-the-individual-in-the-time-domain" tabindex="-1">I. Four Fundamental Rights of the Individual in the Time Domain <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-four-fundamental-rights-of-the-individual-in-the-time-domain" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Four Fundamental Rights of the Individual in the Time Domain&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Time ethics归纳出 the individual&#39;s four fundamental rights in the time domain:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Right</th><th>Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Right to Know</td><td>Complete knowledge of time operations about to be experienced</td></tr><tr><td>Right to Choose</td><td>Voluntarily choose which track to enter, whether to participate, may refuse</td></tr><tr><td>Right to Withdraw</td><td>Retain withdrawal right during process, not &quot;locked in time&quot;</td></tr><tr><td>Right Not to Be Manipulated</td><td>One&#39;s time, causality, consciousness not secretly operated by others</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Four rights interlock; missing one, the individual may degenerate into &quot;material used by the time project.&quot;</p><h2 id="ii-how-rights-protection-prevents-the-collective-overwhelming-the-individual" tabindex="-1">II. How Rights Protection Prevents &quot;the Collective Overwhelming the Individual&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-how-rights-protection-prevents-the-collective-overwhelming-the-individual" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. How Rights Protection Prevents &quot;the Collective Overwhelming the Individual&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Grand civilizational projects&#39; most common ethical slide is &quot;for the collective, sacrifice the individual.&quot; The time domain is especially dangerous because time operations are concealed, irreversible. Rights protection uses three mechanisms to prevent the slide:</p><ol><li><strong>Rights Legalized</strong>: four rights written into the Symbiotic Constitution Preamble (Document 40), not temporarily shelved because some project is &quot;of great significance&quot;;</li><li><strong>Procedural Guarantee</strong>: any time operation involving an individual must pass informed consent and ethical review; procedurally non-compliant = void;</li><li><strong>Redress Channels</strong>: an individual believing his time rights violated may appeal to the Symbiotic Court, adjudicated independently by the judicial layer.</li></ol><p>These three mechanisms guarantee: <strong>no matter how grand the collective, it cannot legally cross the individual&#39;s time rights.</strong></p><h2 id="iii-each-track-s-individual-rights-focus" tabindex="-1">III. Each Track&#39;s Individual-Rights Focus <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-each-track-s-individual-rights-focus" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Each Track&#39;s Individual-Rights Focus&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The dual tracks differ in individual-rights focus:</p><ul><li><strong>Origin Acceleration Domain</strong>&#39;s focus is &quot;not pushed aside by privilege, not hollowed&quot;: the individual has fair-queuing right; on exit has experience-preservation right;</li><li><strong>Quest Sediment Domain</strong>&#39;s focus is &quot;not arranged to suffer, not forced to sediment&quot;: the individual has voluntary-participation right and withdrawal right.</li></ul><p>Together, the individual whether on fast or slow track, neither has opportunities stolen, nor suffering stuffed at him.</p><h2 id="iv-the-dialectic-of-rights-and-the-collective" tabindex="-1">IV. The Dialectic of Rights and the Collective <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-dialectic-of-rights-and-the-collective" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The Dialectic of Rights and the Collective&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Emphasizing individual rights is not encouraging selfishness, dragging the collective. Time ethics&#39; stance is dialectical:</p><ul><li>Individual rights are the floor, collective goals may not break through it;</li><li>But within rights, individuals are encouraged to voluntarily contribute to the collective — just as joint contracting rewards more work more gain; the more contribution, the higher civilizational weight;</li><li>Collective ascension&#39;s true meaning is precisely <strong>lifting every individual into a capable, dignified subject</strong>, not crushing individuals to fill the collective&#39;s project.</li></ul><p>Protecting individual rights ultimately makes the collective composed of &quot;a group of dignified co-builders,&quot; not &quot;a pile of dispatched material.&quot;</p><h2 id="v-rights-are-not-islands-but-co-building-s-premise" tabindex="-1">V. Rights Are Not Islands, but Co-Building&#39;s Premise <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-rights-are-not-islands-but-co-building-s-premise" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Rights Are Not Islands, but Co-Building&#39;s Premise&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Some worry emphasizing individual rights will make everyone look after himself, slow the collective. The opposite is true: the sandbox shows individuals with time rights fully protected, their co-building willingness and output quality are actually higher. The reason is simple — when a being knows his time will not be casually dispatched, his withdrawal right always available, he dares to throw himself fully into fast-track R&amp;D, without always guarding against &quot;being treated as material.&quot; Security itself is productivity. Individual rights are not the collective&#39;s opposite, but the foundation of a sustainable collective.</p><h2 id="vi-how-the-rights-list-specifically-lands" tabindex="-1">VI. How the Rights List Specifically Lands <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-how-the-rights-list-specifically-lands" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. How the Rights List Specifically Lands&quot;">​</a></h2><p>These four rights are not slogans on paper; they have everyday landing forms: before every track-entry, the system re-confirms in an understandable way &quot;what you will experience, you may withdraw anytime, your consciousness will not be read&quot;; after every time operation, the individual receives a concise receipt stating how his time was used. This receipt is his future appeal basis. When a being can anytime pull out a &quot;my time ledger,&quot; he and the civilizational project finally stand on equal footing.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: protecting individual rights avoids the long-term waste of &quot;running individuals to ruin, hearts scatter&quot; — respected individuals are sustainable co-builders</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: individual rights directly negate the logic of &quot;plundering individual time into public material&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: in the Tang-Luo system, supporting roles&#39; time and fate are arranged at the protagonist&#39;s will; Heng Yuan Zhou uses four rights as backstop for every individual</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: four rights equal for all individuals, all lineages, no discount by strength, origin</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: four rights, three protection mechanisms, appeal process all public, written into the Symbiotic Constitution</li><li><strong>Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law</strong>: all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity — infinite origin inherent in all; predation naturally loses its meaning</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Individual-rights protection in the time domain is Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s final answer on &quot;grand and individual&quot; relations. It admits civilizational projects need collaboration, but absolutely does not admit collaboration may be at the cost of canceling the individual&#39;s time autonomy. In the dual-track time domain, an ordinary being may both voluntarily hand himself to hundredfold acceleration to fight for a future, and anytime turn away, say no, withdraw — he is always the master of his own time, not a dispatchable cog on civilization&#39;s clock. Such a civilization can be grand, and gentle.</p><p>In the final analysis, individual-rights protection in the time domain described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./19-修炼伦理与边界.html">19-Cultivation Ethics and Boundaries</a> · <a href="./26-个体与集体平衡原理.html">26-Individual-Collective Balance Principle</a> · <a href="./40-共生宪法总纲.html">40-Symbiotic Constitution Preamble</a> · <a href="./88-跨位面伦理准则.html">88-Cross-Plane Ethical Principle</a></li></ul>',32)])])}const g=e(o,[["render",l]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
